{number: 101}
{title: Thou, My Everlasting Portion}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Thou my everlasting portion,
[F] More than friend or [C] life to me;
All along my pilgrim journey,
[G7] Savior, let me [C] walk with Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Close to [F] Thee, close to [C] Thee,
Close to [G7] Thee, close to [C] Thee,
All a-[F] long my pilgrim [C] journey,
Savior, [G7] let me walk with [C] Thee.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Not for ease or worldly pleasure,
[F] Nor for fame my [C] prayer shall be;
Gladly will I toil and suffer,
[G7] Only let me [C] walk with Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Lead me through the vale of shadows,
[F] Bear me o'er life's [C] fitful sea;
Then the gate of life eternal
[G7] May I enter, [C] Lord, with Thee.
{end_of_verse}
